+# Design
+
+## Direction
+Editorial career strategy: crisp navy canvas, white document cards, blue structure, and gold used only for decisions and forward direction. The visual metaphor moves from archive clutter to a curated evidence case file.
+
+## Layout
+Keep all essential content inside the 120px frame padding and above the footer reserve. Use large, short headlines rather than displaying narration verbatim. Alternate document close-ups, three-card diagnostics, a direction line, an evidence stack, a rewritten bullet comparison, and a final tool handoff.
+
+## Type and color
+Use Proxima Nova with the system fallback. Headlines are 64–88px, supporting copy 34–42px, and labels 22px. Navy is the field, paper white is the main surface, blue organizes information, and gold marks the active insight.
+
+## Motion
+One paused GSAP timeline controls the entire composition. Each timed clip enters with a short upward reveal and exits with a short fade. Document rows and evidence cards stagger within their beat. No infinite motion.
